<div class="info-page">
  <h1>Marketing Dictionary</h1>
  <p>Common digital marketing terms and acronyms explained.</p>

  <dl class="glossary">
    <dt>API</dt>
    <dd>Application Programming Interface — a way for two software applications to communicate.</dd>

    <dt>Bounce Rate</dt>
    <dd>The percentage of visitors who leave a site after viewing only one page.</dd>

    <dt>CPA</dt>
    <dd>Cost Per Acquisition — the cost to acquire one paying customer.</dd>

    <dt>CPC</dt>
    <dd>Cost Per Click — the price paid for each click on an ad.</dd>

    <dt>CPM</dt>
    <dd>Cost Per Mille — the cost per 1,000 ad impressions.</dd>

    <dt>CRM</dt>
    <dd>Customer Relationship Management — tools for managing interactions with customers.</dd>

    <dt>CTR</dt>
    <dd>Click-Through Rate — the ratio of clicks to impressions, expressed as a percentage.</dd>

    <dt>CVR</dt>
    <dd>Conversion Rate — the percentage of users who complete a desired action.</dd>

    <dt>DAU / MAU</dt>
    <dd>Daily Active Users / Monthly Active Users — engagement metrics for apps and platforms.</dd>

    <dt>HEAT</dt>
    <dd>Highest Earning Available Tomorrow — a keyword bidding strategy for search ads.</dd>

    <dt>KPI</dt>
    <dd>Key Performance Indicator — a measurable value that shows progress toward a goal.</dd>

    <dt>LTV / CLV</dt>
    <dd>Lifetime Value / Customer Lifetime Value — the total revenue expected from a customer.</dd>

    <dt>PPC</dt>
    <dd>Pay Per Click — an advertising model where the advertiser pays per click.</dd>

    <dt>ROAS</dt>
    <dd>Return On Ad Spend — revenue generated per dollar spent on advertising.</dd>

    <dt>ROI</dt>
    <dd>Return On Investment — the profitability of an investment relative to its cost.</dd>

    <dt>SEM</dt>
    <dd>Search Engine Marketing — paid advertising on search engines.</dd>

    <dt>SEO</dt>
    <dd>Search Engine Optimisation — improving a site's visibility in organic search results.</dd>

    <dt>SERP</dt>
    <dd>Search Engine Results Page — the page shown after a user performs a search.</dd>

    <dt>UTM</dt>
    <dd>Urchin Tracking Module — parameters added to URLs for campaign tracking in analytics.</dd>
  </dl>
</div>

